      "baseRefName": "main",
      "body": "## What changed\n\n- Complete the offline Python 3.12 base-wheel staging in the Gemma 4 audit, SDK acceptance, inference, and TP4 state notebooks.\n- Add a private official ADK harness task trial using the exact validated submission files and the organizer's wheelhouse and server. The local kaggle-vllm inference path remains separate.\n- Point the current acceptance guide at the already-published SDK 0.3.1 release and record the fresh four-L4 offline Input audit in the paper draft.\n\n## Verified\n\n- Live PyPI, GitHub, and Hugging Face release identity checks pass for SDK 0.3.1 and native vLLM 0.30.0.\n- Private four-L4 offline audit passed: 168/168 locked dependency wheel SHA256 values, exact SDK/native SHA256, and mounted Gemma model files.\n- Official adk-submission 0.2.13 validated the submission directory and compiled its single-model agent.\n- `python -m pytest -q tests/test_release_state.py tests/test_production_acceptance_assets_v030.py`: 14 passed.\n- All six Gemma competition notebooks parse as valid JSON and Python code; the new runner compiles.\n\n## Still pending\n\nThe separate 19-gate SDK 0.3.1 Kaggle acceptance and official agent task trial are running. Gemma inference latency, TP4 checkpoint save/reload, scored submission, and paper conclusions require their own executed evidence. No GPU or agent benchmark pass is asserted here.\n",
