      "baseRefName": "main",
      "body": "## Summary\n- Preserve the published 0.2.0 T4 and 0.3.1 L4 artifacts while preparing the corrected 0.3.2 pure Python SDK.\n- Pin all 168 L4 dependency wheel identities to original publisher sources: 162 PyPI, five PyTorch CUDA 12.9, one FlashInfer. The SDK allowlists HTTPS hosts and verifies every file by exact size and SHA256 before isolated staging. No dependency wheel is proposed for a third-party Hub mirror.\n- Prepare a 16-operation additive Hugging Face plan for two existing native-wheel server-side copies and 14 small metadata/index files. Preserve historic paths.\n- Add a publisher-source audit, legal gate, guarded PyPI workflow, release reports and two output-free manual acceptance notebooks.\n\n## Local verification\n- Python 3.11: 426 passed, 1 skipped; compileall passed.\n- All 168 exact publisher files were identified; 167 checksums were advertised by publisher indexes, and TorchVision's bytes were independently downloaded and SHA256 verified. PyPI's same-named Triton file has a different hash, so the matching PyTorch file is pinned.\n- A live small publisher wheel download passed SHA256. The full 168-wheel local lock and both native wheels were verified in the prior local audit.\n- Two fixed-epoch SDK wheel builds and normalized sdists matched byte-for-byte; Twine passed. These are source-candidate artifacts pending the immutable Hub pin.\n- Both primary notebooks passed nbformat, JSON and Python AST structural checks. Neither notebook was executed by Codex.\n\n## Release blockers\n- The versioned Hugging Face native/metadata namespace is absent, so the SDK immutable revision is unset and public bootstrap fails closed.\n- The native wheel's compiled-component redistribution and notices require documented clearance before the planned public copies. The revised plan does not upload dependency wheels.\n- Hub publication needs explicit user authorization. Final Hub pin/rebuild, approved merge, authorized GitHub/PyPI publication, and fresh user-run four-L4 acceptance remain pending. No 0.3.2 GPU success is claimed.\n\nSee `reports/v032-production-release/20-final-handoff.md`, `21-manual-notebook-paths.md` and `18-production-gates.json`. This PR remains draft for review and performs no Kaggle execution.\n",
